          "type": "text",
          "text": "I've started a research helper. It shows in the sidebar as \"Research: answers hidden inside the collapsed 'Worked' row\", so you can watch or steer it. It runs on Sol, and the thread supervisor will flag it if it stalls.\n\nIt scans every chat from the last 14 days for text that the folded \"Worked\" row hides. It reuses the scripts from the 25 Oct round, so it reads chat history the same way the web UI does. Each hidden message gets one of two labels:\n- **Important:** a question to you, steps to do, a diagnosis, a decision, a warning, a result, a link you need, or the answer itself.\n- **Filler:** \"let me check…\" and the like.\n\nFiller gets counted too. Then the \"you're missing things\" figure comes with an honest share, not just the worst cases.\n\nYou'll get three things in `projects/openclaw-ios/tmp/hidden-worked-20261109/`:\n- **`REPORT.md`:** totals by model and by type of hidden content, then 10–15 of the strongest examples. Each shows what you saw next to what was hidden, plus a few cases where only filler was hidden.\n- **`hits.json`:** every hidden message it found.\n- **About 6 screenshots** in the 25 Oct style: collapsed, expanded, and annotated with blue boxes for hidden content and red for the important part. Each is shrunk to 1 MP, with full-size originals kept.\n\nPrivacy rules I gave it:\n- Nothing is posted anywhere.\n- Tokens, keys, token URLs, phone numbers and email addresses are blacked out in every image, not just the annotated copies. That fixes last time's mistake.\n- Work sessions are preferred; anything about health, money or family is skipped.\n\nI'll send you the headline numbers when it reports back."
