      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The report is ready, but the screenshots aren't done. It's at `projects/openclaw-ios/tmp/hidden-worked-20261109/REPORT.md`, and the folder is on the `marv1SSD` share you just mounted.\n\n**Headline numbers** (26 Oct to today, 83 sessions):\n- **1,206 messages** were hidden inside 537 \"Worked\" rows.\n- **555 of them (46%)** were filler: \"let me check…\" and the like.\n- **355 of the 537 rows (66%)** hid something important. The most common types were warnings or caveats (252 messages), results or numbers (177), steps for you to do (104) and diagnoses (76).\n- **By model:** Sol hid important text in 73% of rows, Astra in 63%, and Opus in 42%.\n\nThe 66% comes from automatic keyword rules, so it's an estimate rather than an audited figure. The report says so.\n\n**13 examples were checked by hand.** Each shows what you saw next to what was hidden, and it notes where the final answer repeated the hidden point, so it's not cherry-picked. Two of them argue your case well:\n- **#2 (Opus):** the whole answer about the clicky1 audio cut was in the fold, file table included. The visible final message was something else.\n- **#11:** a direct question asking you to approve a flash was hidden.\n\n**Why there are no screenshots:** the helper couldn't get a browser that was logged in to the Control UI. Direct access asked for proxy authentication, and the tailnet page wouldn't load in Chrome. It correctly didn't work around the login.\n\nYour browser on the pmac is logged in. Pick one:\n- **I drive your browser:** I open each of the six conversations in your Chrome and take the shots myself. That takes over your screen for a few minutes.\n- **You keep your screen:** you take the shots, and I do the annotation, the blacking-out of tokens and URLs, and the 1 MP resize."
